ealth Action Plan 2004&#x02013;2010 (2004/2132 (INI)) PE 349.889v02&#x02013;00. Brussels:Commission of the European Communities.</citation></ref><ref id="b9-ehp0115-000983"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Dalston</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Faustman</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Ginsberg</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Fenner-Crisp</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Olin</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Sonawane</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>A framework for assessing risks to children from exposure to environmental agents</article-title><source>Environ Health Perspect</source><volume>112</volume><fpage>238</fpage><lpage>256</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14754580</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b10-ehp0115-000983"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group><name><surname>Dol</surname><given-names>CP</given-names></name><name><surname>Haffner</surname><given-names>MEA</given-names></name></person-group> 2001. House Statistics in the European Union 2001. Helsinski:Finnish Ministry of Environment,</citation></ref><ref id="b11-ehp0115-000983"><citation citation-type="other"><collab>ECTP (European Construction Technology Platform)</collab> 2005. Strategic Research Agenda for the European Construction Sector. Achieving a Sustainable and Competitive Construction Sector by 2030. Draft Version, 1 June 2005. Available: <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.ectp.org">http://www.ectp.org</ext-link> [accessed 5 July 2006].</citation></ref><ref id="b12-ehp0115-000983"><citation citation-type="other"><collab>EU</collab> 2005. Activities of the European Union. Summaries of Legislation. Ban on Smoking in Places Open to the Public. Brussels:European Union. Available: <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://europa.eu/scad