ame><surname>Iversen</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Nielsen</surname><given-names>KF</given-names></name></person-group><year>1999</year><article-title>Microfungal contamination of damp buildings&#x02014;examples of risk constructions and risk materials</article-title><source>Environ Health Perspect</source><volume>107</volume><issue>suppl 3</issue><fpage>505</fpage><lpage>508</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10347000</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b19-ehp0115-000983"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group><name><surname>Haffner</surname><given-names>MEA</given-names></name><name><surname>Dol</surname><given-names>CP</given-names></name></person-group> 2000. Housing Statistics in the European Union. Delft, the Netherlands:OTB Research Institute for Housing, Urban and Mobility Studies, Delft University of Technology.</citation></ref><ref id="b20-ehp0115-000983"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group><name><surname>Ineichen</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group> 1993. Homes and Health: How Housing and Health Interact. London:E &#x00026; FN Spon.</citation></ref><ref id="b21-ehp0115-000983"><citation citation-type="other"><collab>IOM (Institute of Medicine)</collab> 2000. Clearing the Air: Asthma and Indoor Air Exposures. Washington, DC:National Academy Press.</citation></ref><ref id="b22-ehp0115-000983"><citation citation-type="other"><collab>IOM (Institute of Medicine)</collab> 2004. Damp Indoor Spaces and Health. Washington, DC:National Academy Press..</citation></ref><ref id="b23-ehp0115-000983"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Jacobs</surname><given-names>DE</given-names></name><name><surname>Kelly</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Sobolewski</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>Linking public health, housing and indoor environmental policy: successes and challenges at local and federal agen